  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The edit-mode preview moves real scene objects, so it has to put everything
    back exactly, step aside for saves, play mode and recompiles, and never run game
    code. These tiles check that, plus how previews chain and how the buttons behave
    in play mode.


    <b>Using this board:</b> select a tile. Its Inspector shows
    these directions at the top, with Select buttons for the objects to watch, and
    its UI Animation Player underneath. Badges in a tile''s corner say what it needs:
    <color=#FF9E5E>PREVIEW</color> (the Play buttons, out of play mode), <color=#FF9E5E>PLAY
    MODE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>INSPECTOR</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>SCENE VIEW</color>,
    <color=#FF9E5E>CONSOLE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>POP-OUT</color> (an animation''s
    own window).


    In play mode: right-drag pans, the wheel zooms, Tab steps
    through tiles, Home shows them all.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f44eed8c3b5782c408b32755e14054d5, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 5947266920940028113, guid: f44eed8c3b5782c408b32755e14054d5, type: 2}
